{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966794,"nonce":"ILVE1C1F3/NI1Hh76G8XYJPpp8A=","title":"CSS classes are hashed NOWHERE in blinc_layout/src/diff.rs, and","message":"Two durable facts about the incremental renderer, established while reviewing PR #62 (keyed child reconciliation):\n\n**1. CSS classes are in NO hash.** `grep -i class crates/blinc_layout/src/diff.rs` returns nothing: neither `compute_element`, `compute_element_tree`, nor `compute_topology_tree` hash `element_classes()`. So a class-only change is invisible to the diff engine and never triggers a rebuild on its own. Class changes reach the tree only because some *other* prop changed and dragged a rebuild along. This is why class staleness bugs are permanent once they happen: nothing re-triggers.\n\n**2. `update_render_props_in_place_boxed` (renderer/build/diff.rs) skips two things the full-rebuild paths do.** It recurses into children and refreshes props, but it does NOT:\n- re-register CSS classes (`element_registry.register_classes` / `clear_classes` + `base_styles.remove` on change). `apply_stylesheet_base_styles_for_subtree` then resolves via `class_to_nodes_index()` and applies the OLD classes.\n- refresh `render_node.element_type` (`determine_element_type_boxed`). The topology hash covers only element-type discriminant, `element_id`, text content+font_size, svg/image `source`, child count. It does NOT cover svg `tint`/fill/stroke, text color/weight, image tint/filter, or canvas `render_fn` (canvas is hashed nowhere) — so those go stale on any in-place update.\n\n`renderer/build/subtree.rs` does BOTH correctly and its comments name the exact bug (\"Without this, adding/removing classes (e.g. cn-sidebar-item--active) wouldn't take effect\" / \"Without this, visual-only rebuilds leave stale element data\"). The fix is to mirror those ~8 lines into `update_render_props_in_place_boxed`; verified it fixes the failure and keeps all 749 blinc_layout lib tests green. Patch kept at `scratchpad/keep-pr62-fix.patch` (session-local).\n\n**Repro (branch-neutral, no GPU):** build `div().child(div().id(\"alice\").w(100.).class(\"row\")).child(div().id(\"bob\").w(200.).class(\"row\"))`, then `incremental_update` to a list that inserts a third keyed child AND adds `.class(\"row--active\")` to alice. Assert `element_registry().class_to_nodes_index()[\"row--active\"].len() == 1`. Query by CLASS, not `query_by_id` — see below.\n\n**Related pre-existing bug on main (fixed by PR #62):** `rebuild_children_in_place` never called `register_element_ids_walk`, so after any child-count change `query_by_id(\"alice\")` returns None for surviving items. Also, main's full rebuild LEAKS class registrations (destroyed nodes stay in `class_to_nodes_index`, so `row` counted 5 for 3 nodes).\n\nSame family as gotcha class styles dropped on subtree rebuild and gotcha refresh stateful clobbers state styles. See also gotcha canvas closures have side effects.","files":null}]}